# Netlify response headers (Vite copies this into dist/ at build time).
#
# Content-Security-Policy
# - No 'unsafe-inline' in script-src: this is what stops Netlify's injected
#   "Powered by Netlify" badge from rendering (it runs as an inline script in
#   an iframe). See https://docs.netlify.com/manage/projects/powered-by-netlify-badge/
# - 'self': the app's own bundle in /assets.
# - blob: the 3D "OXY" title (troika-three-text) lays out text in Web Workers it
#   creates from blob: URLs and loads code into with importScripts(blob:).
#   Without it the whole 3D hero fails to render. worker-src alone is not
#   enough, because importScripts inside the worker is checked against script-src.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self' blob:
